<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 891)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Deliver the media from Share This Review.</b> A <b>Media</b> row in the live review: <b>Deliver the Media&#8230;</b> lists the services, opens the package sheet with that destination chosen, and shows the delivery&#8217;s progress and result here.</li>
<li><b>The package sheet says where the delivery will go</b> before you press the button &#8212; the full path, resolved for this review &#8212; and the button reads &#8220;Deliver to Suite&#8221;. The folder is revealed after.</li>
<li><b>The review connects to the delivery.</b> With a link (a zip&#8217;s own file link, when the service&#8217;s policy allows one) every clip&#8217;s source link is the zip and a seat fetches it on its own. On Suite or a folder, the path is the source for people who mount it. Invited-only on a cloud service: the invite says where it is and the person downloads it and drops it on Asobi&#8217;s window. A local synced-folder path is never handed out as a link any more.</li>
<li>Settings &#8250; Deliveries: the template on its own full-width line; the preview uses a real job.</li>
<li><b>The invite&#8217;s &#8220;Their media&#8221; rethought:</b> plain rows &#8212; stream review copies, a package sent through Asobi, <b>the package delivered to a service</b> (new: the invite says where it is, and the guest is told to download it and drop it on the window when it isn&#8217;t a link), or links to the originals &#8212; with <b>Deliver the Media&#8230;</b> right there when nothing is delivered yet.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
